WARP PORTABLE (UNOFFICIAL BUILD)
================================

WHAT THIS IS
------------
This is an unofficial, portable build of the open-source Warp terminal
(the "OSS" channel). It is not made, signed off or supported by Warp or
Denver Technologies, Inc. Please do not ask them for support with it.

HOW TO START
------------
1. Unzip the whole archive anywhere you can write to, for example the
   Desktop or a USB stick. Paths with spaces are fine.
2. Double-click warp-oss.exe.

No administrator rights are needed and there is nothing to install.

WHERE YOUR DATA IS STORED
-------------------------
Settings, themes, history and logs are kept in the "data" folder next to
warp-oss.exe. It is created the first time you start the app.

  - To move everything to another PC: copy the whole WarpPortable folder.
  - To remove everything: delete the WarpPortable folder.

The folder must be writable. If it is not, Warp shows an error instead of
storing data somewhere else.

FIRST-RUN WARNING (WINDOWS SMARTSCREEN)
---------------------------------------
This build is not code-signed. If the zip was downloaded with a browser,
Windows may show "Windows protected your PC" when you start it. Click
"More info", then "Run anyway".

To avoid the warning, do one of these:
  - copy the zip to the PC over a USB stick, a network share or RDP, or
  - before unzipping, run this in PowerShell:
        Unblock-File -Path <path to the zip>

Computers managed with AppLocker or WDAC policies may refuse to run
unsigned programs. If that happens, this build cannot be used there.

SIGNING IN
----------
Warp's AI and cloud features need a Warp account and an internet
connection. The terminal itself works without signing in: choose
"Skip for now" on the sign-in screen.

In this portable build the browser sign-in does not return to the app
automatically. To sign in:
  1. Start the sign-in and log in in your browser.
  2. Copy the link the browser page tries to open. It starts with
     warposs://
  3. In the same Warp window, click "Click here to paste your token from
     the browser" and paste the link.

Your sign-in does not move with the folder. On another PC or under another
Windows user you have to sign in again.

OTHER LIMITS
------------
  - No automatic updates. A new version is a new zip.
  - warposs:// links (for example shared sessions or Warp Drive links)
    do not open the app.
  - Installing the Claude Code, Codex or Gemini plugins from inside Warp
    writes into those tools' own folders in your user profile.
  - "Start Warp at login" is not available.
  - Warp offers PowerShell (and WSL / Git Bash if installed) as shells;
    cmd is not available as a Warp shell.

